%description:
A UE's node id is below the range of background UEs, which starts at 4097. NR UEs get the ids
2049, 2050, ... by default, so the 2049th NR UE of a network got 4097: the channel model then
took it for a background UE and gave it no shadowing, and the MAXCI scheduler treated it as one,
without a message. The id is set directly here, which reaches the same check without 2049 UEs.
It is an error at initialization.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.ue[0].nrMacNodeId = 4097

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
macNodeId 4097 is in the range of background UEs (4097 and up)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
